    dct:description "A modern phylogenetic-isolation operationalization permits a strong partial test. Fossil completeness is inadequate to establish severe extinction for all isolated groups." ;
    rdfs:comment "Proposed test with existing data: Define aberrance as high phylogenetic isolation, then test whether isolated extant clades have low extant richness, high pairwise disparity, and fossil evidence of formerly greater diversity. Joint evidence supports their interpretation as extinction relicts." ;
